mqvpn (0.16.0-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * feat(multipath): add the reverse direction of PATH_LABEL sync -- an
    operator-pinned per-(user,iface) weight/dscp_mask (from "path_policy"
    or a live set_path_weight/set_path_dscp_mask _by_iface call) can now
    be pushed SERVER -> CLIENT and adopted into that client's own uplink
    scheduling, so a server-side, per-user override no longer requires a
    separate action on the router. New PushPathLabels key ([Multipath]
    INI / push_path_labels JSON), --push-path-labels CLI flag, and
    mqvpn_config_set_push_path_labels() library API; off by default and,
    unlike SyncPathLabels, requires both sides to opt in. Only ever
    pushes an operator-pinned value, never an echo of that same client's
    own announcement, so it cannot loop with the existing sync.
  * feat(config): add a server-only "path_policy" JSON config array --
    persisted per-(user,iface) weight/dscp_mask overrides, applied the
    first time that user's connection announces a PATH_LABEL for the
    matching iface, so an operator override now survives a server
    restart and a client reconnect instead of only living in the
    control socket's in-process state; new
    mqvpn_config_add_path_policy() library API. Takes effect only under
    the wrr/wrtt/dscp schedulers, same as the live
    set_path_weight/set_path_dscp_mask calls it persists.
  * feat(sched): add the dscp policy-routing scheduler -- routes each
    packet by the inner IP header's DSCP class to whichever assigned path
    currently has the best RTT (min-RTT tie-break; falls back to plain
    MinRTT across every path for untagged traffic or a class with no
    usable assigned path); new set_path_dscp_mask client/control-API
    command.
  * feat(multipath): automatically sync per-path weight and DSCP mask
    from client to server -- set_path_weight/set_path_dscp_mask on the
    client alone now biases both directions, via a PATH_LABEL capsule
    that survives path_id churn across reconnects; an operator's
    explicit server-side call still wins (asymmetric control).
  * feat(config): add a SyncPathLabels key ([Multipath] INI /
    sync_path_labels JSON) and a --no-sync-path-labels CLI flag to turn
    the above sync off; gates each side's own half independently
    (server: stop auto-adopting the client's report; client: stop
    announcing it at all), so either side alone is enough to decouple
    them; new mqvpn_config_set_sync_path_labels() library API.
  * feat(offload): add UDP GSO (capability probe, run formation, TX batch
    send with sendmmsg fallback, sticky-fallback logging) and UDP GRO
    (sockopt helper, segmented receive with cmsg parsing) on client and
    server path sockets; new UdpGso/UdpGro config keys (INI+JSON parity)
    and A/B netem benchmark scripts.
  * feat(stats): expose the new UDP offload counters via get_stats;
    assert them in the control API e2e.
  * feat(server): defer the datagram flush when a batched send is
    registered, flushing before close/destroy and on every egress path;
    fix svr_flush_deferred_sends being defined only inside the
    egress-only block.
  * feat(logging): annotate xquic's terse "|err:NNN|" report fields
    (CONNECTION_CLOSE transport / H3 / QPACK wire codes) with a symbolic
    name, e.g. "|err:0x106(H3_FRAME_ERROR)|" -- new
    mqvpn_xquic_err_names.h name table mirrored from xqc_errno.h, wired
    into cb_xqc_log_write on both client and server; grows the log line
    buffer 512 -> 600 bytes so the annotation can't truncate the tail of
    xquic's own report lines.
  * fix: harden udp_offload result codes and the batch cap; preserve UDP
    GRO across a netlink path re-add; pin the exact cmsg length and
    hard-error errno preservation.
  * build: bump the shared library SOVERSION to 3 (single definition,
    shared with the batched-send condition check).
  * chore(deps): bump the xquic fork seven times in total, for the DSCP
    scheduler, the GRO/GSO wiring, and the server defer-flush fix; bump the
    com.google.devtools.ksp Android dependency.
  * test: dscp scheduler, PATH_LABEL capsule, and control-socket unit
    tests; ci_bench_dscp_verify.sh integration check; SyncPathLabels and
    PushPathLabels config (INI+JSON parity) and control-API unit tests.
  * docs: document the dscp scheduler, the client->server weight/DSCP
    auto-sync, the SyncPathLabels opt-out, the persisted path_policy
    override, and the PushPathLabels server->client push (README).
  * ci: always wipe and re-clone the pinned BoringSSL checkout in every
    workflow that builds it (deb-package, perf-fec-reinjection,
    test-path-api, test-pending-regression, test-standby-backup, test-cc,
    test-ciphers) -- xquic now vendors its own BoringSSL submodule, so the
    recursive checkout step already populates that path, sometimes with a
    stale or shallow copy, before the workflow's own pinned-commit clone
    step runs.

